From: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ACS: scan for all links of an AP MLD with one request

The links of an AP MLD share one wiphy, and the kernel runs one scan per
wiphy at a time. If several links use ACS, each link scans for itself,
and every link after the first one gets -EBUSY and retries every
ACS_SCAN_RETRY_INTERVAL seconds. The ACS of three links then takes
three full scans and the retry delays, and every retry logs two lines
at info level.

Scan for all links of the AP MLD that are in ACS with one request:

- acs_request_scan() adds the channels of every partner link that is in
  ACS and waits for a scan, and gives those links the scan callback.
- acs_scan_complete() fetches the survey once. Every link of the scan
  keeps its scan callback until then, and the survey event hands the
  survey to each of them, whichever link the driver reports it on.
  Each link keeps the channels of its own band.
- Each link then counts the scan, and continues from the event loop:
  the links that need more scans with the next request, the others
  with the channel study. EVENT_SCAN_RESULTS may still go on to call
  the scan callback of the partners when the results reached a link
  that did not scan, so a request started from the callback would be
  taken as completed at once.
- A link that the scan of a partner link includes waits at most
  ACS_SCAN_WAIT_TIMEOUT seconds for its results, and then scans for
  itself. The results can be lost when the partner link is torn down.
- acs_cleanup() drops the scan callback of ACS, so that a link that is
  disabled during its scan does not block the scans of its partner
  links.

A driver that scans its radios in parallel can then serve all links
with one scan.

The partner scan check of hostapd_driver_scan() moves into
hostapd_mld_partner_scanning(). A scan that has to wait for a partner
link is expected, so log it at debug level.

Signed-off-by: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
[nbd: continue the requesting link from the event loop as well, keep
 its scan callback until the survey is fetched, add the wait timeout of
 a partner link and the scan callback reset in acs_cleanup()]
